  "scope_and_limits": [
    "Registry entries remain raw leaked descriptor pointers; raw RuntimeType::register calls do not create an owning handle for the new descriptor.",
    "Each macro-backed RuntimeTyped class keeps a static owning handle, and each registered child descriptor owns one handle to its parent.",
    "Generic NCollection H-array/H-sequence and MAT list/node descriptor specializations use a separate TypeId-keyed static owner cache; the Standard_Type registry remains raw.",
    "Handle::from_static and static_type_handle/dynamic_type_handle provide explicit owning paths while preserving static_type and dynamic_type borrowed return types.",
    "This does not reproduce native descriptor destruction or explicit registration lifetime semantics: Rust registry descriptors are leaked to retain stable addresses."
  ]
